<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-volvo</span></b> , volvi,
			vŏlūtum, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to roll</i> or <i>tumble about</i> (syn. voluto). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem in luto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 4, 4, 38</span></i>
			.—Mid., <i>to roll one's self</i>, <i>to roll</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in suo pervoluta sanguine,</span>”
				<i>weltering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 8, p. 207, 22</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to turn over</i> a
			book, <i>to read</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Smyrnam incana diu saecula pervoluent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					95, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to be very busy</i>
			or <i>much engaged</i> in any thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut in iis locis pervolvatur animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 35, 149</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
